{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-01T08:16:08.304Z","data":{"text":"Task 1 is complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Triggers** (`src/core/status/steering.ts`)\n- `SteeringTriggerName` now includes `conflict` and `requirement_changed`.\n- A change-level `regressed/change.md` maps `sync_conflict` → `conflict`, `requirement_changed` → `requirement_changed`, and `sync_verify_red`/`verify_red`/`verify_path_missing` → `regression`.\n- Added and exported `isDefaultBranchTrigger(trigger)` (true for `conflict`, `requirement_changed`, and `regression` with `sync_verify_red`).\n\n**Stop reasons** (`sync-stop.ts`, `sync-specs.ts`, `sync-verify.ts`)\n- `SyncStopReason` gained `requirement_changed` and `sync_verify_red`.\n- `assertRequirementsUnchanged` throws `requirement_changed` with the new `run osq plan <id> to revise the plan against <branch>` message.\n- Red verify/check throws `sync_verify_red`; `skipVerify` runs no command but still appends `synced`.\n\n**Files** (`sync-files.ts` new, `sync-main.ts`)\n- `readRequirementsBase` reads `.run/requirements-base`, else `.run/base`, else null; the requirement check uses it.\n- `readEvents`/`restoreEvents` moved into `sync-files.ts`; `sync-main.ts` is 243 lines.\n- `syncWithDefaultBranch` takes `options: { skipVerify?: boolean } = {}`; the conflict stop now says to run `osq plan <id>` and restarts the branch.\n\n**Watcher** (`worktree-run.ts`)\n- `WorktreeHaltReason` gained `requirement_changed` and `sync_verify_red`; `sync-run.ts` unchanged.\n\n**Tests**\n- Updated expected messages/reasons in `vcs-sync`, `vcs-sync-active`, `vcs-land`, and `change-check` tests.\n- Added `tests/steering-sync.test.ts` covering all eight named scenarios.\n\nBoth the task verify (`node --import tsx --test tests/steering-sync.test.ts`, 8/8 pass) and the proposal verify (`pnpm verify`) pass, and the result file is written to `openspec/changes/129-default-branch-steering/.run/results/1.md`."}}
